          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the perpendicular bisector can be constructed using the simplest geometric tools — an unmarked ruler and a compass. We will use only these two tools for all the other geometric constructions in this chapter, unless there is a need for drawing lines of specific lengths in standard units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.398,
            0.314,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.431,
            0.846,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. When constructing the perpendicular bisector, is it necessary to have the same radius for the arcs above and below XY? Explore this through construction, and then justify your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.495,
            0.846,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "["
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Any point that is of the same distance from X and Y lies on the perpendicular bisector."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.538,
            0.846,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We can draw the whole line if any two of its points are known.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.582,
            0.848,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Is it necessary to construct the pairs of arcs above and below XY? Instead, can we construct both the pairs of arcs on the same side of XY? Explore this through construction, and then justify your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.646,
            0.847,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. While constructing one pair of intersecting arcs, is it necessary that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.664,
            0.713,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "we use the same radii for both of them ? Explore this through construction, and then justify your answer."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
